    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **255 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the structured audit event in the one place the create pipeline already audits owners: `AuditOwnerCreated` (the `audit` step in `owners.POST.yml`, which runs after `SaveOwner` so the persisted id is available).\n\nChanges to `src/main/java/.../rest/function/owner/AuditOwnerCreated.java`:\n\n- **Kept** the existing human-readable audit line unchanged.\n- **Added** an immutable structured JSON event emitted on the same `AUDIT` logger:\n  `{\"seq\":\u2026,\"ownerId\":\u2026,\"customerCode\":\u2026,\"membershipLevel\":\u2026,\"event\":\"OWNER_CREATED\"}`\n- **`seq`** is a process-wide `AtomicLong` (`SEQUENCE.incrementAndGet()`), giving a monotonically increasing integer across all creates.\n- **Primary-identifier evolution**: the `customerCode` value is read through a single `primaryIdentifier(Owner)` helper. Today it returns `owner.getCustomerCode()`; when the customerCode is later unified into a memberId, that one method is the sole switch point and the event value tracks whatever the primary identifier becomes (the JSON key stays `customerCode` as the spec fixes it).\n- JSON is built with a small `quote(...)` escaper so the event is well-formed even if a value ever contains special characters.\n\nThe new `AcceptanceTest.coreEventCarriesIdAndIdentifier` passes \u2014 the AUDIT capture confirms a line like `{\"seq\":1,\"ownerId\":11,\"customerCode\":\"NSW-16E6609E\",\"membershipLevel\":1,\"event\":\"OWNER_CREATED\"}` \u2014 and no existing tests regressed.",
